## 🛡️ 3. Memory & Functionality Invariants (Zero-Loss Guarantee)

When developers ask if cleaning `.git` risks losing **functionality** or **memory**:
1. **Agent Memory & SCONES**:
   - SCONES knowledge graph (`scones_memory.db`), agent memories (`MEMORY.md`, `USER.md`), skills (`skills/`), and Obsidian vault (`docs/vault/`) are **active files on disk**.
   - They do NOT depend on historical packfile blobs. Cleaning packfiles leaves all active memory 100% intact.
2. **Production Functionality**:
   - Active codebase in `core/`, `apps/`, `services/`, `packages/` is defined by `HEAD`. Historical blobs (like deleted binaries or old backups) have zero runtime role.

